      "side": 1,
      "message": "we can\u0027t just flip polarity here because the usb_pd_protocol keeps track of polarity and uses that for other things. for example, when you disconnect cable, protocol layer sets USB muxes to NONE on the polarity in use.\n\nso, I think you need to add a function to the protocol layer to flip the polarity. the protocol layer can verify that the other CC channel has the correct voltage (meaning it checks that you have two CC lines), and then it switches the polarity and calls board_set_usb_mux() appropriately.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 265,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 265,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "3380d59357546d9275fe20804b52443ceb1f4c84",
